WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:04.880
To ensure my agent has the necessary

2
00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:07.120
context to use the open- source

3
00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:08.880
libraries I've chosen to use, I must

4
00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:10.639
make sure I've installed all the usage

5
00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:13.759
specifications for every direct

6
00:00:10.639 --> 00:00:16.080
dependency in my project.

7
00:00:13.759 --> 00:00:18.240
I'm going to ask Claude Code to discover

8
00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:20.880
which direct dependencies I'm using and

9
00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:24.080
find a usage spec for each one in turn.

10
00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:26.400
Claude Code uses Tessle's MCP search

11
00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:28.480
tool to look for each usage spec in

12
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:30.160
Tessle spec registry, attempting to

13
00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:32.800
match the package name we're using in my

14
00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:34.640
project with a corresponding usage spec.

15
00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:36.160
Once matched, it will install the

16
00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:38.399
correct version them from the spec

17
00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:41.920
registry to my local file system again

18
00:00:38.399 --> 00:00:44.559
via the Tessle MCP server.

19
00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:46.640
On my local file system, the Tessle.json

20
00:00:44.559 --> 00:00:49.120
file shows the project dependencies for

21
00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:51.200
which we have matched usage specs. The

22
00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:52.960
knowledge MD maps these to the local

23
00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:55.600
specs we have now installed on our file

24
00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:58.079
system stored in my project. The

25
00:00:55.600 --> 00:01:00.239
index.mmd file serves as the root usage

26
00:00:58.079 --> 00:01:03.120
spec linking to all other usage specs

27
00:01:00.239 --> 00:01:04.640
for that open source library.

28
00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:07.040
I've now given my agent the knowledge

29
00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:09.280
and context it needs to code effectively

30
00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:13.200
with all my project dependencies using

31
00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:13.200
Tessle's usage specs.
